  "supported": [
    "A root-relative1024 value revision performs12 parent compact-identity filename-discovery entries, independent of N, plus one union identity check. The12 entries traverse the full parent file population before choosing payload files.",
    "Measured warm source discovery dominates fixed-E latency at1m:52.800s of60.130s. Small changed-layer checks stay~0.054\u20130.058s while F grows64x.",
    "Zero warm available admissions separate repeated native discovery from fresh filesystem validation. Warm unobserved controls are close to observed timings, so the wrapper is not the measured dominant cost."
  ],
  "refuted": [
    "Fresh file admission alone explains the warm-session root-edit bottleneck: warmavailable calls are zero.",
    "Payload volume E alone determines this operation cost: E stays1024 while input file count and latency grow."
  ],
  "inconclusive": [
    "No mathematical growth exponent inferred from3 timings: N/F are coupled, filesystem caches not flushed, one case per size, and strict tests/tiny metadata checks may overlap.",
    "No end-to-end contention extrapolation: these sibling-root requests read original large-layer occurrences. Latest-generated occurrences may live in small incoming layers. Contention opens a fresh publisher session each batch; warm here reuses one session."
  ],
  "practical_next_change": "Reduce full-parent file discovery at the shared record-store owner using existing physical member metadata, if exact or conservative identity bounds can be produced and independently validated. Preserve compact-identity fallback where bounds cannot exclude a file; do not add another payload cache. Also avoid repeating discovery for the same bounded requested identities across source validation stages when existing admitted data can be reused. This is a proposed change, not an adopted implementation.",
